name 'building-data-driven-systems-preassessment-q7_2025'

question 'Which piece of code correctly defines a JavaScript object representing a car?'

wrong '`let car = ["Toyota", "Camry", 2022];`'
right '`let car = { brand: "Toyota", model: "Camry", year: 2022 };`'
wrong '`let car = "brand: Toyota, model: Camry, year: 2022";`'
wrong '`let car = brand("Toyota") + model("Camry");`'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 4

Objects use curly braces {} and key-value pairs separated by colons. Option A is an array, and Option C is a string.
MARKDOWN
